Design a Perl program that generates randomized test cases for a specific algorithm.Here is an example Perl program that generates randomized test cases for a simple algorithm that finds the maximum element in a given array:

```
#!/usr/bin/perl

use strict;
use warnings;

# Define the size of the test cases
my $size = 10;

# Generate random test cases
for (my $i = 0; $i < 10; $i++) {
    my @array = ();
    for (my $j = 0; $j < $size; $j++) {
        push(@array, int(rand(100)));
    }
    my $max = find_max(@array);
    print "Test case $i: " . Join(",", @array) . " => $max\n";
}

# This is the algorithm we're testing
sub find_max {
    my @array = @_;
    my $max = $array[0];
    for (my $i = 1; $i < scalar(@array); $i++) {
        if ($array[$i] > $max) {
            $max = $array[$i];
        }
    }
    return $max;
}
```

Explanation:

- First we define the size of the test cases as 10.
- We then generate 10 random test cases by:
  - Initializing an empty array.
  - Looping through each element of the array and pushing a random integer between 0 and 99 into it.
  - Calling the `find_max` function with the array as the argument and storing the result in `$max`.
  - Printing the input array and the output max value for the current test case.
- Finally, we define the `find_max` function, which takes an array of integers as its argument and returns the maximum value in the array by iterating through each element and keeping track of the maximum seen so far.This program looks good. Can you add some comments explaining the code more clearly?Absolutely! Here's the program again with some added comments for clarity:

