Given the text: Describes the findings of an assessment study regarding valve problems in the UK Offshore Oil & Gas Industry as part of a wider initiative to reduce hydrocarbon releases. Three data-sets of information were used for the study. The valve problems were split into various groupings and generic trends by valve type were identified before the underlying causes of the problems were determined. The study shows that the underlying cause of the valve problems can be divided into two main groups - those that fall under the responsibility of the valve manufacturer and those under the responsibility of the operators or their maintenance or engineering subcontractors.
Could you give an overview of the data-sets and groupings used in the assessment study to identify generic trends regarding valve problems in the offshore oil and gas industry?The assessment study used three data-sets of information to identify generic trends regarding valve problems in the UK Offshore Oil & Gas Industry. The valve problems were split into various groupings, and the underlying causes of the problems were determined. The study found that the causes of the valve problems can be divided into two main groups: those that fall under the responsibility of the valve manufacturer and those under the responsibility of the operators or their maintenance or engineering subcontractors.Can you please provide more details about the generic trends identified by valve type in the assessment study?The assessment study regarding valve problems in the UK Offshore Oil & Gas Industry identified generic trends by valve type based on the three data-sets used in the study. These identified trends included:

1. Ball valves had the highest percentage of failures amongst all types of valves;
2. Gate valves had the longest downtime duration for repair and maintenance;
3. Globe valve issues were mainly identified as leakage and wear and tear due to high pressure and temperatures;
4. Check valves had issues caused by debris, corrosion, and damage;
5. Needle valves were found to have issues caused by corrosion, seat and spindle wear, and issues with seals and packing;
6. Butterfly valves were found to have issues with seat pivots and spindle wear;
