GET /my_index/_search/
{
   "aggs": {
      "unique_count": {
         "cardinality": {
            "field": "field_name.keyword"
         }
      }
   }
}
```

2. Date Histogram Aggregation Technique: The Date Histogram Aggregation Technique provides a time-based aggregation of data. This technique can be used to find the distribution of events over time.

```
GET /my_index/_search/
{
   "aggs": {
      "events_over_time": {
         "date_histogram": {
            "field": "timestamp",
            "interval": "1h",
            "format": "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss"
         }
      }
   }
}
```

3. Range Aggregation Technique: The Range Aggregation Technique provides an aggregation of data within a specified range. This technique can be used to find the distribution of data within a specified range.

```
GET /my_index/_search/
{
   "aggs": {
      "age_range": {
         "range": {
            "field": "age",
            "ranges": [
               { "to": 20 },
               { "from": 20, "to": 30 },
               { "from": 30 }
            ]
         }
      }
   }
}
```

4. Geo Bounds Aggregation Technique: The Geo Bounds Aggregation Technique provides the boundary of values in the geo-point data. This technique can be used to find the extent of the region covered by the dataset.

```
GET /my_index/_search/
{
   "aggs": {
      "location": {
         "geo_bounds": {
            "field": "location_field"
         }
      }
   }
}
```

5. Percentile Ranks Aggregation Technique: The Percentile Ranks Aggregation Technique provides the percentile rank of each value in the dataset. This technique can be used to find the distribution of each value in the dataset.

```
GET /my_index/_search/
{
   "aggs": {
      "prate": {
         "percentile_ranks": {
            "field": "values_field",
            "values": [20, 30, 40, 50, 60]
         }
      }
   }
}
```

These are just a few examples of advanced aggregation techniques that you can use in your Elasticsearch database operations. Elasticsearch offers a wide range of powerful and flexible aggregation techniques that can help you analyze and understand your data.

