166. Shuffle an array in JavaScript:To shuffle an array in JavaScript, you can use the Fisher-Yates (aka Knuth) shuffle algorithm.

Here is an example implementation:

```
function shuffleArray(array) {
  for (let I = array.length - 1; I > 0; i--) {
    const j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));
    [array[i], array[j]] = [array[j], array[i]];
  }
  return array;
}
```

This function takes an array as input and returns the shuffled array.

How it works:

- Start at the last element of the array (i.e., index `array.length - 1`).
- Pick a random index `j` between 0 and `i` (inclusive).
- Swap the elements at index `i` and `j`.
- Move to the next element by decrementing `i`.
- Repeat steps 2-4 until the first element is reached.

