Create a PowerShell script that enables a user to manage Windows services on remote machines using PowerShell Remoting. The script should include functions to start, stop, restart, disable or enable a specified service on multiple remote machines, and should also provide error handling and logging capabilities. The script should have a clear and readable format with commented code and should be easy to customize to suit different environments.### Overview

This PowerShell script allows a user to manage Windows services on remote machines using PowerShell Remoting. The script includes functions to start, stop, restart, disable or enable a specified service on multiple remote machines. Additionally, the script provides error handling and logging capabilities. The script is designed to be easy to customize to suit different environments with clear and readable format and commented code.

### Prerequisites

- Windows PowerShell 5.0 or later
- Remote PowerShell enabled on the target machines
- Administrative access to the target machines
- WinRM enabled and configured
- Firewall configured to allow PowerShell Remoting traffic

### Configuration

- Define the list of machines in the `$machines` array.
- Update the `$service` variable to the name of the target service.
- Ensure that the user account running the script has administrative access to the target machines.

### Script Usage

```powershell
.\Manage-ServicesRemotely.ps1
```

- The script will prompt for credentials to authenticate to the remote machines.
- The script menu options allow user to start, stop, restart, disable or enable the service.
- The script provides error handling and logging capabilities.

### Script Details

```powershell
# Define the list of machines
$machines = @(
    "machine1",
    "machine2",
    "machine3"
)

# Define the name of the service to manage
$service = "W32Time"

# Define the log file path
$logFile = "C:\Logs\Manage-ServiceRemotely.log"

# Function to start the service
Function Start-ServiceRemotely ([string]$machineName) {
    Write-Host "Starting service $service on machine $machineName" -ForegroundColor Yellow
    try {
        $session = New-PSSession -ComputerName $machineName -Credential $cred
        Invoke-Command -Session $session -ScriptBlock { Start-Service $using:service }
        Write-Log "$service started on $machineName"
        Write-Host "$service started on $machineName" -ForegroundColor Green
    } catch {
        Write-Log "Failed to start $service on $machineName. Exception: $_"
        Write-Host "Failed to start $service on $machineName" -ForegroundColor Red
    } finally {
        Remove-PSSession -Session $session
    }
}

# Function to stop the service
Function Stop-ServiceRemotely ([string]$machineName) {
    Write-Host "Stopping service $service on machine $machineName" -ForegroundColor Yellow
    try {
        $session = New-PSSession -ComputerName $machineName -Credential $cred
        Invoke-Command -Session $session -ScriptBlock { Stop-Service $using:service }
        Write-Log "$service stopped on $machineName"
        Write-Host "$service stopped on $machineName" -ForegroundColor Green
    } catch {
        Write-Log "Failed to stop $service on $machineName. Exception: $_"
        Write-Host "Failed to stop $service on $machineName" -ForegroundColor Red
    } finally {
        Remove-PSSession -Session $session
    }
}

# Function to restart the service
Function Restart-ServiceRemotely ([string]$machineName) {
    Write-Host "Restarting service $service on machine $machineName" -ForegroundColor Yellow
    try {
        $session = New-PSSession -ComputerName $machineName -Credential $cred
        Invoke-Command -Session $session -ScriptBlock { Restart-Service $using:service }
        Write-Log "$service restarted on $machineName"
        Write-Host "$service restarted on $machineName" -ForegroundColor Green
    } catch {
        Write-Log "Failed to restart $service on $machineName. Exception: $_"
        Write-Host "Failed to restart $service on $machineName" -ForegroundColor Red
    } finally {
        Remove-PSSession -Session $session
    }
}

# Function to disable the service
Function Disable-ServiceRemotely ([string]$machineName) {
    Write-Host "Disabling service $service on machine $machineName" -ForegroundColor Yellow
    try {
        $session = New-PSSession -ComputerName $machineName -Credential $cred
        Invoke-Command -Session $session -ScriptBlock { Set-Service -Name $using:service -StartupType Disabled }
        Write-Log "$service disabled on $machineName"
        Write-Host "$service disabled on $machineName" -ForegroundColor Green
    } catch {
        Write-Log "Failed to disable $service on $machineName. Exception: $_"
